  grid: 11x11 [observed]; interior 9x9
  frame: 1-pixel solid border, single non-black color (6 [observed])
  background: single color filling interior, differs from frame (7 [observed])
  sprites:
    count: 4
    colors: 4 distinct non-black colors, all different from frame and background
    shape: asymmetric T — a 4-cell bar + a 3-cell perpendicular crossbar at position 1 or 2 (not center); bbox 3x4 or 4x3
    direction: crossbar closer to the pointed end; position 1 = points toward bar start, position 2 = points toward bar end
    orientation: each can be horizontal (bar along row) or vertical (bar along col), mix varies freely
    axis_uniqueness: each sprite's bar row/col is distinct — no two sprites share the same axis line
    placement: entirely inside the frame (rows 1..H-2, cols 1..W-2); sprites may be 4-adjacent to frame or to each other
    endpoint_constraint: pointed and opposite frame cells (axis projected to both frame edges) must all be distinct — 8 unique frame cells total
  no_black_in_input: black (0) never appears in the input
  output_same_size: true
  transform: |
    For each sprite, project its bar axis to both frame edges.
    Paint the pointed-end frame cell with the sprite's color.
    Paint the opposite-end frame cell black (0).
