0019: 
0020:     Input structure
0021:     - The dominant color forms solid walls around one or more rectangular cavities.
0022:     - A unique most common non-wall color is the empty cavity color.
0023:     - Each cavity contains exactly one other color, arranged as one copy of a repeat tile.
0024: 
0025:     Rule
0026:     - For each 4-connected non-wall cavity, take the bbox of its seed color as the tile.
0027:     - Repeat that tile across the entire cavity, preserving the phase set by the seed's current position.
0028:     - Leave wall cells unchanged and leave tile-empty positions as the empty cavity color.
